"""Direct reader and feature adapter for the T4 scene format.

T4 data is not a serialized benchmark sample. A scene is a
directory containing ``derived/scalars.npz``, ``derived/frames.pack``, an
ordered ``derived/cam_names.json`` and raw camera/LiDAR files under
``data/``.  Future agent GT is stored as the variable ``gt_boxes`` and
``gt_labels`` fields in that same ``derived/frames.pack``. This module keeps
that raw T4 directory format at the adapter boundary and emits the small
tensor dictionaries consumed by the existing training loop.

The implementation follows the validated T4 sample contract:

* 10 Hz frames, 30 reader-context frames plus the current frame (the default
  feature path consumes the current status row);
* T4 LiDAR points are ``[x, y, z, intensity, ring_or_time]``;
* the default camera resize follows the historical ``[W, H] =
  [1148, 672]`` contract, emitted by this reader as ``[H, W] = [672, 1148]``;
* map tensors are read from the per-frame bundle in the ego frame;
* future targets are sampled at 0.5 s (indices 5, 10, ..., 40) and converted
  from global ``(x, y, cos(yaw), sin(yaw))`` into the current ego frame.
  The raw 80-frame future window is retained only for oracle-label assembly;
  it is not a history input.

No external package import is required at runtime. The two small compressed
container readers below mirror the public T4 file contracts. Keeping them here
makes the adapter self-contained for deployment.
"""

